<title>GERMANY: Viag - 1997 profits to at least match 1996.</title>
<headline>Viag - 1997 profits to at least match 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified utility Viag AG said on Friday it expected its profits for 1997 would match or rise slightly from 1996 levels.</p>
<p>The firm also said that its expected sales to continue to rise over the course of this year.</p>
<p>Group net profits for full-year 1996 fell to 1.060 billion marks from 1.320 billion marks. Pre-tax profit in the first quarter of 1997 was 674 million marks, up from 668 million marks a year ago.</p>
<p>--Clifford Coonan, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
